      [ ] 8b follow-up (user visual feedback round 1):
         User: sprites mostly render, but at some player rotations
         (esp. 45/135 deg) they vanish or come out partial in
         WIDTH, sometimes background walls draw over them; plus
         three extra doomguys at the E1M1 start.
         BUG FIX (sprite vanish/partial at rotation angles):
         drawtwosided's textureless window advance (cclip = fctop,
         fclip = flbot+1) was UNGATED, but vanilla only does
         ceilingclip = yl-1 / floorclip = yh+1 when
         markceiling/markfloor (r_segs.c:315/345), which are false
         when both sides share the plane - same floor z/pic/light
         (r_segs.c:536-544; sky-sky ceilings are z-equal after the
         worldtop=worldhigh hack; closed doors force both true).
         At shared-plane portals vanilla leaves the clip OPEN while
         we closed it to the seg's floor/ceiling edge row: sprites
         behind stand on that same plane and project PAST the
         edge row (feet below a shared floor line; when the shared
         floor was above the eye flbot < 0 drove fclip negative
         and blanked the whole sprite column) - exactly the
         rotation-dependent vanish/partial-width and walls-over-
         sprites symptoms (which segs are on screen depends on
         view angle).  addline now computes markfloor/markceiling
         with the vanilla formula (sec/back sector fields; the
         existing sky hack in drawtwosided no longer needs to
         guard the ceiling advance - the gate does it) and passes
         them to drawtwosided; the advance is gated, and cclip/
         fclip are clamped to [0..h] at the solid[] store (PLAN
         porting-note requirement; fclip<=cclip is a closed column
         either way).  Vanilla raw-source basis: r_segs.c 440-575
         (markfloor/markceiling), 285-355 (clip stores).
         BUG FIX (three extra doomguys at spawn): game.b
         spawnmapthing spawned EVERY player start (t.typ <= 4 ->
         spawnplayer), so co-op starts 2-4 became mobjs.  Vanilla
         R_SpawnMapThing only turns playeringame slots into
         players; single-player has start 1 only.  Now types 2-4
         return without spawning (type 1 still spawns).
