          addline's markfloor/markceiling implemented vanilla's
          shared-plane compare (r_segs.c:536-560) + closed-door force
          but NOT the view-plane gates that follow in the same
          function (r_segs.c:630-642): front floor >= viewz ->
          markfloor false; front ceiling <= viewz (non-sky) ->
          markceiling false.  At steps/pits/ledges seen from below/
          above the textureless clip advance closed rows vanilla
          leaves open, and the drawseg snapshot then clipped sprites
          behind (feet vanish; the wall shows through where the
          sprite should be).  Validated BEFORE editing
          (/tmp/opencode/markgate_check.py): port marks vs vanilla
          marks over all two-sided sides x all reachable eye heights
          on E1M1..E1M9 (4564 sides) -> 42764 floor + 25453 ceiling
