          BUG FIX (wall light banding): drawtwosided computed the
          per-column light index but assigned wrow only at x == lx1,
          so whole segs shaded with the first column's row.  Vanilla
          (r_segs.c:260-263) picks dc_colormap per column as rw_scale
          steps.  Now assigned every column (1S loop already was).
          BUG FIX (drawseg pool exhaustion): addline never culled
          occluded segs (no R_ClipSolidWallSegment/R_ClipPassWallSegment
          equivalent), so fully-hidden segs burned pool slots; real
          frames saturated the 256 pool (E1M5 demo: ds 256 on every
          sample) and later visible segs - walls and sprite clips -
          were dropped entirely.  addline now skips segs whose
          [lx1,lx2] is entirely closed in solid[] (first-open >=
          one-past-last = vanilla ceilingclip >= floorclip), exactly
          the ranges vanilla never sends to R_StoreWallRange.  Skip
          is pixel-exact: closed columns draw nothing (yt/yb clamp
          to empty), markplane drops empty strips, advances keep the
          column closed; culled mids match vanilla (never recorded).
